sec.p:
For each protein g in sample s, we first calculated the area-based abundance in parts per million:


AreaPPMg,s= Area g,s∑g Area g,s×10
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle _{g, s}=\frac{\text { Area }_{g, s}}{\sum_{g} \text { Area }_{g, s}} \quad \times 10$$\end{document}



This value was then log2-transformed:


Ag,s=log2⁡( AreaPPM g,s+1)
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle A_{g, s}=\log _2\left(\text { AreaPPM }_{g, s}+1\right)$$\end{document}



To correct for differences in immunoprecipitation efficiency across samples, we computed a loading normalization factor Ls for each sample s, defined as the median log2 PPM of all identified Mediator subunits M in that sample:


Ls=medianm∈M(Am,s)
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle L_{s}=\operatorname{median}_{m \in M}\left(A_{m, s}\right)$$\end{document}



The normalized abundance of each protein was then obtained by subtracting this Mediator-derived normalization factor:


Rg,s=Ag,s−Ls
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle R_{g, s}=A_{g, s}-L_{s}$$\end{document}



Finally, the bait-preferential score for each protein was defined as the difference between its normalized abundance in the MED16 IP and the mean of its normalized abundances in the other three Mediator bait IPs (MED1, MED12, CDK8):


Score=Rg,MED16−mean(Rg,MED1,Rg,MED12,Rg,CDK8)
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle =R_{g, \text { MED16 }}-\operatorname{mean}\left(R_{g, \text { MED1 }}, R_{g, \text { MED12 }}, R_{g, \text { CDK8 }}\right.$$\end{document}



A positive score indicates enrichment in the MED16 IP relative to the other three Mediator baits. Candidate proteins of interest were further filtered by the following criteria: detection in at least two of three replicates of the target bait; maximum unique peptide count ≥ 2; detection in at least one additional Mediator bait; exclusion of Mediator/Pol II subunits, ribosomal proteins, histones, keratins, and common contaminants; and annotation with transcription or DNA-binding functions using GO terms from org.Hs.eg.db and GO.db, requiring either transcription regulator activity or DNA binding combined with a transcription-related biological process.
